    <GaugingStation location="Cockfield" name="Brett" number="36009">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">'Essex' profile gauging a small, rural, close to natural, catchment with Upper Chalk covered with Boulder Clay.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Modular limit of 0.66m theoretically derived; secondary instrument to record non-modular flows installed in 2003. Lack of gaugings at high flows. One rating applied across period of record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">'Essex' profile (modified Flat V Crump weir). No spillway.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">No POT data are presented for this station as they have no non-modular flow correction applied. AMAX data have been corrected, but in some cases can be below the daily flow as these are not corrected. Naturalised flows from 1969 to 1976, only minimal adjustments needed since. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2020 (WINFAP Files v9).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Natural to within 10% at Q95.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Upper Chalk completely covered with Boulder Clay. Rural, predominantly arable land.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">N</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Good fit to gaugings." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Non-modularity, with adjustments to AMAX series but implicit uncertainty that makes flows unsuitable above QMED." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
